### Container lifecycle management
$ docker ps   (running containers)
NAMES      IMAGE                                 STATUS          PORTS
lab2-app   devops-lab2-app:2.0.0                 Up 8 minutes    0.0.0.0:5000->5000/tcp, [::]:5000->5000/tcp
minikube   gcr.io/k8s-minikube/kicbase:v0.0.51   Up 13 minutes   127.0.0.1:44620->22/tcp, 127.0.0.1:44621->2376/tcp, 127.0.0.1:44622->5000/tcp, 127.0.0.1:44623->8443/tcp, 127.0.0.1:44624->32443/tcp

$ docker stop lab2-app
lab2-app
$ docker ps -a --filter name=lab2-app   (stopped container still exists)
NAMES      STATUS
lab2-app   Exited (137) Less than a second ago

$ docker start lab2-app
lab2-app
$ docker restart lab2-app
lab2-app
$ curl http://localhost:5000/health   (container back up)


